{"strongs": "H6242", "word": "עֶשְׂרִים", "translit": "es.rim", "root": "עשר", "morph": "H:N", "pos": "noun plural indeclinable", "gloss": "twenty", "definition": "עֶשְׂרִים 315 noun plural indeclinable (a) twenty (ancient plural of עֶשֶׂר Prä BAS i. 376 ; Late Hebrew = Biblical Hebrew; Arabic ; Assyrian ešrâ; Sabean עשרי Hom Chrest. 48 ; Ethiopic Aramaic עשרין , ; Nabataean עשרין ); — I. as cardinal: 1. without other number: \\ \\ a. usually followed by singular noun (especially שָׁנָה , אִישׁ , אַמָּה , etc.) Gen 31:38 ; 1Sam 14:14 ; Exod 38:18 + 64 t., + עֶשְׂרִים אֶלֶף 20,000 1Chr 18:4 + 7 t. + Ezek 45:1 (reading עֶשְׂרִים אָ֑לֶף , see עֶשֶׂר 2 b ). \\ \\ b. followed by plural noun 2Sam 3:20 ; Exod 36:23 ; Exod 36:24 ; Exod 36:25 + 4 t. \\ \\ c. followed by singular noun collective 1Kgs 5:3 . \\ \\ d. plural noun precedes Gen 32:15 (twice in verse); Gen 32:16 ; 2Chr 3:3 + 6 t. \\ \\ e. noun omitted Gen 18:31 (twice in verse) ( ׳ הָע ), 1Kgs 6:2 + 6 t., as predicate Exod 27:10 (twice in verse); Exod 27:11 (twice in verse) + 4 t. feminine + בָּאַמָּה Zech 5:12 . 2. + other number: \\ \\ a. with units, usually 20 + (with וְ ) unit + singular noun Judg 10:2 ; Judg 10:3 ; 1Kgs 14:20 + 58 t. (including 20 + 1 * 1000, etc., 27 t.); noun omitted Josh 15:32 + 2 t. predicate; less often unit + 20 + singular noun Gen 11:24 ; Exod 38:24 ; Num 8:24 (all P ) + 27 t.; unit + 20 + בָּאַמָּה Ezek 40:21 ; Exod 26:2 ; Exod 36:9 (both P ). \\ \\ b. 20 + unit + plural noun Num 7:8 (twice in verse) ( P ), 1Chr 2:22 + 3 t. Chronicles \\ \\ c. plural noun + 20 + unit Josh 19:30 (twice in verse); 1Chr 12:29 ( van d. H. v. 1Chr 12:28 ). \\ \\ d. c. hundreds, 20 usually following; followed by singular noun 1Kgs 9:14 ; Gen 6:3 ; Deut 31:2 + 7 t.; noun omitted 2Chr 3:4 ; Ezra 2:32 = Neh 7:35 20 + 100 (noun omitted) Num 7:86 . \\ \\ e. plural noun + 100 + 20 1Chr 15:5 ; 1Chr 15:6 — compare further מֵאָה . II. as ordinal: 1. 20 alone, ׳ בִּשְׁנַת ע in the twentieth year 1Kgs 15:9 + 4 t.; noun omitted Num 10:11 + 3 t. 2. a. 20 + unit + ns. Ezek 29:17 ; Ezek 40:1 . \\ \\ b. ns. + 20 + unit Hag 1:15 ; 2Chr 7:10 +; ns. + unit + 20 Exod 12:8 בִּשְׁנַת + 20 + unit 1Kgs 16:10 , etc. — See references below עֶשֶׂר .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6445')\">BDB6445</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H6242')\">H6242</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H6235')\">H6235</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6444')\">BDB6444</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6446')\">BDB6446</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>עֶשְׂרִים</bdbheb><sub>315</sub> <b>noun plural indeclinable</b> (a) <highlightword>twenty</highlightword> (ancient plural of <bdbheb>עֶשֶׂר</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Prä')\">Prä<sup>BAS i. 376</sup></lookup>; Late Hebrew = Biblical Hebrew; Arabic <placeholder4121/>; Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>ešrâ;</highlight></transliteration> Sabean <bdbheb>עשרי</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hom')\">Hom<sup>Chrest. 48</sup></lookup>; Ethiopic <placeholder4122/> Aramaic <bdbarc>עשרין</bdbarc>, <placeholder4123/>; Nabataean <bdbheb>עשרין</bdbheb>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>I.</b> as cardinal: </div><div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> without other number: <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> usually followed by singular noun (especially <bdbheb>שָׁנָה</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אִישׁ</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אַמָּה</bdbheb>, etc.) <ref ref=\"Gen 31:38\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"38\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"38\" onclick=\"bcv(1,31,38)\">Gen 31:38</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 14:14\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(9,14,14)\">1Sam 14:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 38:18\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"38\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"38\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(2,38,18)\">Exod 38:18</ref> + 64 t., + <bdbheb>עֶשְׂרִים אֶלֶף</bdbheb> 20,000 <ref ref=\"1Chr 18:4\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(13,18,4)\">1Chr 18:4</ref> + 7 t. + <ref ref=\"Ezek 45:1\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(26,45,1)\">Ezek 45:1</ref> (reading <bdbheb>עֶשְׂרִים אָ֑לֶף</bdbheb>, see  <bdbheb><reflink>עֶשֶׂר</reflink></bdbheb> <b>2 b</b>). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> followed by plural noun <ref ref=\"2Sam 3:20\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(10,3,20)\">2Sam 3:20</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 36:23\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"36\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"36\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(2,36,23)\">Exod 36:23</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 36:24\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"36\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"36\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(2,36,24)\">Exod 36:24</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 36:25\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"36\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"36\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(2,36,25)\">Exod 36:25</ref> + 4 t. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>c.</b> followed by singular noun collective <ref ref=\"1Kgs 5:3\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(11,5,3)\">1Kgs 5:3</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>d.</b> plural noun precedes <ref ref=\"Gen 32:15\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(1,32,15)\">Gen 32:15</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Gen 32:16\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(1,32,16)\">Gen 32:16</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 3:3\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(14,3,3)\">2Chr 3:3</ref> + 6 t. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>e.</b> noun omitted <ref ref=\"Gen 18:31\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(1,18,31)\">Gen 18:31</ref> (twice in verse) (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הָע</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"1Kgs 6:2\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(11,6,2)\">1Kgs 6:2</ref> + 6 t., as predicate <ref ref=\"Exod 27:10\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(2,27,10)\">Exod 27:10</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Exod 27:11\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(2,27,11)\">Exod 27:11</re